WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.708
PRIYANKA VERGADIA:
Have you ever wondered

00:00:01.708 --> 00:00:04.160
if you could just
upload an FAQ document

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:06.560
and a chatbot would
magically be created

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:08.570
to answer those questions?

00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:11.030
Well, keep watching
to find out more.

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:13.220
Welcome to
"Deconstructing Chatbots."

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:15.930
I'm Priyanka Vergadia,
and in this episode,

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:19.589
we will explore Dialogflow's
Knowledge Connector feature.

00:00:19.589 --> 00:00:23.012
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:28.810
At the time of this
recording, Knowledge Connector

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:31.840
is a beta feature
within Dialogflow.

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:34.810
Knowledge Connector
complements the defined intents

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:38.690
by parsing documents
such as FAQs or articles

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:41.920
to find questions and responses.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:44.380
Questions are added
as training phrases,

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:47.650
and answers are
added as responses.

00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:51.460
To configure them, you define
one or more knowledge bases,

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:54.070
which are collections
of documents.

00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:57.310
At the time of this
recording, CSV and HTML files

00:00:57.310 --> 00:00:59.290
are supported for ingestion.

00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:01.450
Let's jump into our
Dialogflow console

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:03.170
and see how to set it up.

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:06.650
Use an existing agent
or create a new one.

00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:08.560
If you do not know how
to create an agent,

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:10.780
refer to the third
episode of the series

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:13.420
where we are building an
appointment scheduler.

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:15.190
Because this is a
beta feature, we

00:01:15.190 --> 00:01:20.200
start by going to the gear icon
and enabling the beta options.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:23.790
Now we are ready to create
our Knowledge Connector.

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:26.410
Select the Knowledge
beta from the left pane

00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:29.080
and click Create Knowledge Base.

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:31.450
Give it a name and save.

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:34.510
Now we need a knowledge
document that we can use

00:01:34.510 --> 00:01:37.030
to auto-generate the chatbot.

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:40.450
I have opened this Compute
Engine FAQ here as a sample.

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:42.730
Let's use this one.

00:01:42.730 --> 00:01:44.770
Let's go back to
our Dialogflow agent

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:47.950
and create our first
Knowledge Connector.

00:01:47.950 --> 00:01:50.800
I'm calling it
Compute Engine FAQ.

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:52.450
Select a Knowledge type.

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:54.350
It is FAQ in this case.

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:55.690
Select a MIME type.

00:01:55.690 --> 00:01:58.090
In this case, it is HTML file.

00:01:58.090 --> 00:02:01.400
And we add a URL
to this document.

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:05.380
Once you have
filled, click Create.

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:07.240
And just like that,
the Knowledge Connector

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:09.880
has created the FAQ chatbot.

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:12.870
Let's click on our
Compute Engine FAQ.

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:15.730
We see that the questions
are parsed into requests

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:18.380
and responses neatly.

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:22.520
Click on Add Response to
enable the automated responses.

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:25.340
That's all, just save.

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:29.450
Before you test, make sure
you have enabled the chatbot.

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:32.900
Click on the checkbox beside
the name of the FAQ and click

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:34.880
Enable.

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:36.740
Now we are ready to test.

00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:38.870
In the simulator
on the right, query

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:43.430
your Dialogflow agent with, what
is pricing for compute engine?

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:45.740
And you will see a
response from the bot.

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:48.860
Try out more examples
like, how do I get support?

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:52.250
You will notice that I did not
type the exact same question

00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:56.390
from the FAQ, and it still gets
mapped to the correct intent.

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:58.790
That's the beauty of
Knowledge Connector.

00:02:58.790 --> 00:03:03.320
Today, we learned how to create
an FAQ chatbot from an HTML

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:06.560
or CSV file in less
than two minutes.

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:09.140
Try this awesome beta
feature and create

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:13.100
some chatbots to answer those
FAQ questions automatically.

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:16.160
Once you do, don't forget to
share the experience with us

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:17.270
in comments.

00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:20.210
I hope to see you in the next
episode of "Deconstructing

00:03:20.210 --> 00:03:20.900
Chatbots."

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:22.610
If you liked this
video and would

00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:24.860
like to see more
such content, don't

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:27.020
forget to like and
subscribe to our channel.

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:30.370
[MUSIC PLAYING]

